      },
      {
        "id": "D",
        "text": "b < c < a",
        "image": ""
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "A",
    "explanation": "Explanation: Nitrobenzene (b) is strongly deactivated due to -M/-I of nitro group. Chlorobenzene (a) is weakly deactivated due to -I > +R of chlorine. Anisole (c) is strongly activated due to +R of methoxy group. Hence, the increasing order of reactivity is b < a < c. Option A.",
